# CleanShot web — environment variables
#
# Both vars are NEXT_PUBLIC_* and therefore baked into the client bundle.
# This is intentional per Phase 3 design (decision D in the cutover):
#   - NEXT_PUBLIC_API_KEY is visible to anyone viewing source.
#   - Server-side defenses are origin pinning (Cloud Run validates Origin
#     against ALLOWED_ORIGINS) and Cloud Armor rate-limit policies.
#   - Real auth (Auth0/Clerk/WorkOS) lands when actual user accounts arrive
#     — not in v1.
#
# If you ever upgrade to a server-side proxy pattern (Phase 3.5), introduce
# CLEANSHOT_API_KEY (no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix) consumed only by route handlers
# under app/api/, and rotate the public key out of the bundle.

NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_KEY=local-dev-key
